  "query_preview": "..(This Evening Through Thursday)\nIssued at 1202 PM MDT Thu Oct 15 2026\n\nCurrent upper air analysis shows upper trof axis draped across \nthe Northern Plains. Attendant sfc front is pushing through the \nCWA with 3 hr pressure rises of 3-4 mb behind it. The pressure \nrises and cold air advection is supporting widespread gusty \nnorthwest winds, especially across the western SD plains. Stations\nacross western SD have begun to report gusts of 45-55 mph, these \nwinds should continue through this afternoon into late evening \nbefore diminishing overnight as the front exits the region. While \na few gusts up to 60 mph are possible, the majority of gusts \nshould be around 45 to 55 mph.\n\nCAA and clearing skies will result in widespread freezing/sub- \nfreezing temps tonight into Friday for much of the area. Freeze \nWarning remains in effect for most of the forecast area tonight \ninto tomorrow morning.\n\nUpper ridging builds over the western CONUS by Friday into this \nweekend. Expecting above average highs this weekend into early \nnext week with elevated fire wx conditions. Next chances for \nprecip arrive later next week as another trof deepens across the \nwestern US, though it's still too far out to determine any \nspecifics about precip chances or timing.",
